{
 "texts": {
  "Grace-0": "Akple and Ademe are traditional Ghanaian dishes, particularly popular among the Ewe people of the Volta Region.",
  "Grace-1": "Ayisha Modi has issued a stern warning to popular Ghanaian fetish priestess, Nana Agradaa.",
  "Grace-2": "Following his installation, he has assumed the stool name Nii Otanka Okaija Akraman.",
  "Grace-3": "Team Ghana were disqualified on infringement in the final changeover from Joseph Oduro Manu and Joseph Amoah.",
  "Comfort-0": "They are skipper Christian Amoah, Winifred Ntumi and Sandra Mensimah Owusu.",
  "Comfort-1": "He is the son of the late Emma Naa Ameley Tagoe and hails from the Adanse Royal lineage.",
  "Comfort-2": "Didi began his youth career with Bolga Soccer Masters at Bolgatanga in the Upper East Region of Ghana.",
  "Comfort-3": "The arrests occurred in Blorkorfe and Awakpedome, both suburbs of Adidome in the Central Tongu District.",
  "Mercy-0": "This ruling was widely interpreted as a validation of Nii Adama Latse's claim to the Ga Mantse title.",
  "Mercy-1": "Adams Atidana Oliver won gold while Ofori Appiah Joel and Samuel Owusu won silver and bronze respectively.",
  "Mercy-2": "Juabenhene Nana Otuo Sereboe II was among the chiefs who pleaded on their behalf.",
  "Mercy-3": "Chirano is a mining community in the Bibiani Ahweso Bekai Municipality in the Western North.",
  "Patience-0": "The consignment originated from Kwahu Fodoa and was en route to Togo through Aflao.",
  "Patience-1": "Following the fight, Ghanaians have been recalling the similar annihilation Bastie Samir handed to Bukom Banku.",
  "Patience-2": "The NPP's Solomon Kwame Asumadu is contesting the Akwatia seat against the NDC's Bernard Bediako.",
  "Patience-3": "Esa Payin gave birth to Bediako Ntim, who became the successor of Opon Payin.",
  "Emmanuel-0": "Volivo to Dorfor Adidome Bridge across the Volta River has been revived.",
  "Emmanuel-1": "Shatta Bandle was born Idris Firdaus, a Northerner from a small village called Karaga.",
  "Emmanuel-2": "The Saviour Church of Ghana has named a school at Bonwire after her, Nana Konadu Saviour School.",
  "Emmanuel-3": "Bofoakwa Tano have severed ties with coach Frimpong Manso after four months at the helm, the club announced.",
  "Isaac-0": "Member of Parliament for Bawku Central, Mahama Ayariga has reported that three more people were killed in Bawku.",
  "Isaac-1": "Ghanaian musician Stonebwoy has taken legal action against politician and entertainment critic, Baba Sadiq.",
  "Isaac-2": "Ghana legend and former Asante Kotoko star Opoku Afriyie has passed away.",
  "Isaac-3": "Ghanaians on social media are eulogising veteran Highlife musician, Nana Kwame Ampadu.",
  "Ebenezer-0": "The Information Minister, Kojo Oppong Nkrumah says government is working to stabilise the cedi.",
  "Ebenezer-1": "The Adom TV Fufuo Party is underway at the forecourt of The Multimedia Group at Kokomlemle in Accra.",
  "Ebenezer-2": "A court has ordered Marwako Fast Food in Accra to pay over a million Ghana cedis in damages.",
  "Ebenezer-3": "Sarkodie, Shatta Wale and Stonebwoy are undoubtedly three of Ghana's biggest musicians.",
  "Bright-0": "Odododiodio MP Edwin Nii Lante Vanderpuye, will not return to Parliament after the expiration of his current term.",
  "Bright-1": "Ghanaian singer Kofi Mante has acknowledged Bisa Kdei's influence on the highlife music genre.",
  "Bright-2": "Former President, John Dramani Mahama has condemned the killing of Al Jazeera journalist Shireen Abu Akleh.",
  "Bright-3": "Ghanaian legal luminary Tsatsu Tsikata has proposed a solution to Ghana's recurring Cedi depreciation."
 },
